# =============================================================================
#  THALASSES VILLAS — REDESIGN
#  What is excluded and why is documented in EXCLUDED-MANIFEST.md.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Secrets. Nothing with a credential in it, ever. ------------------------
# This repository is PUBLIC. No key, token, connection string or certificate
# may ever be committed. The enquiry form's mail provider key, when it exists,
# goes into Vercel environment variables — never into a file in this tree.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
.vercel/
.netlify/
secrets.json
credentials.json

# ---- Dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/releases

# ---- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Test + QA artefacts (all regenerable) ----------------------------------
# `qa/screens` is 217 MB of full-page screenshots at six breakpoints, rebuilt by
# `npm run qa:screens`. `qa/walkthrough` and `qa/diagnose` are scratch.
# The evidence that is REFERENCED by the deliverable docs is kept:
#   qa/phase3, qa/acts, qa/curation, qa/font-ab.png
qa/screens/
qa/walkthrough/
qa/diagnose/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# ---- OS / editor ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# =============================================================================
#  PHOTOGRAPHY
#  Only images the content inventory or the source actually references are
#  tracked. Everything else in public/images is excluded, listed in
#  EXCLUDED-MANIFEST.md, and recoverable from content/assets-manifest.json.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Ruled off the site by the owner ----------------------------------------
# Stock photography, a branded third-party product shot, two public places and
# one frame that is almost certainly a different property, plus two quarantined
# frames awaiting provenance. `localImage()` already resolves each of these to
# null, so they can never render — they have no reason to be in the repository
# either. Reasons and provenance: content/excluded-images.json.
